  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "It is a sunny day. Pat is a small boy. He is in the garden with Lily. \"What color is Pip?\" asks Lily. \"Pip is brown,\" says Pat. \"Good!\" says Lily. She smiles at Pat. \"Now find a gray thing.\" Pat looks at the wall. He looks at the door. He looks at the table. \"I can not see it,\" says Pat.",
      "Pip sits next to the gray wall. \"Woof, woof!\" says Pip. Pat looks at Pip. A small thing is next to the wall. It is gray, too! \"It is a baby mouse!\" says Lily. \"Is it Squeaky?\" asks Pat. \"Yes, it is!\" says Lily. Squeaky has two small black eyes.",
      "Pat has some bread in his bag. He gives it to Squeaky. Squeaky eats the bread. \"He is happy,\" says Pat. Pat gives some bread to Pip too. The bread is brown. Pip is brown. Squeaky is gray. \"I like colors!\" says Pat."
    ],
    "summary": "Pat plays a color game with Lily in the garden. Pip shows them a gray baby mouse, and Pat gives it some bread.",
